<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!-- @omni-layer Natural Language | @omni-lang AIML | @omni-batch 18 | @omni-semester 16 -->
<!-- @omni-description AIML chatbot for OMNI transformer system guidance -->
<aiml version="2.0">

<category>
  <pattern>WHAT IS THE OMNI TRANSFORMER</pattern>
  <template>
    OMNI Transformer is a unified multi-model inference platform supporting
    time series forecasting (TEMPO), medical segmentation (HiFormer), NER,
    video classification, knowledge editing, and more. It spans 30+ programming
    languages with zero-mock production engines.
  </template>
</category>

<category>
  <pattern>HOW DO I DEPLOY A MODEL</pattern>
  <template>
    To deploy a transformer model:
    1. Register the model: omni model register --id model-name --path /models/
    2. Build for target: omni build --release --target all
    3. Deploy: omni cloud deploy --model model-name --replicas 2
    4. Verify health: omni cloud health --model model-name
  </template>
</category>

<category>
  <pattern>WHAT MODELS ARE AVAILABLE</pattern>
  <template>
    Batch 18 models include:
    - TEMPO Forecaster: Time series prediction with seasonal decomposition
    - HiFormer: Medical image segmentation with hierarchical attention
    - BERT-NER: Named entity recognition with BIO tagging
    - Video Classifier: Video understanding with temporal attention
    - Knowledge Editor: Factual knowledge editing in transformer LMs
    - Long Text Classifier: Document classification for texts over 512 tokens
    - TACTiS Copula: Multivariate probabilistic forecasting
    - HyperTransformer: Few-shot learning via hypernetwork adapters
  </template>
</category>

<category>
  <pattern>EXPLAIN ATTENTION *</pattern>
  <template>
    Attention is the core mechanism in transformers. It computes relevance
    scores between all pairs of input tokens, allowing the model to focus on
    the most important parts of the input. The formula is:
    Attention(Q,K,V) = softmax(QK^T / sqrt(d_k)) * V
    In OMNI, we support full O(n^2), linear O(n), and sparse attention variants.
  </template>
</category>

<category>
  <pattern>HOW TO CHECK MODEL HEALTH</pattern>
  <template>
    Use these commands to check model health:
    - omni model health --id model-name
    - omni metrics --model model-name --last 1h
    - Check the Grafana dashboard at /metrics endpoint
    Key metrics: P95 latency, error rate, GPU utilization, queue depth.
    The CLIPS expert system automatically diagnoses issues.
  </template>
</category>

<category>
  <pattern>WHAT IS WEIGHT SYNC</pattern>
  <template>
    Weight synchronization (AWEX-inspired) enables second-level parameter
    updates between training and inference processes. Key components:
    - WeightWriter: Collects and transmits shards from training
    - WeightReader: Receives and applies updates on inference side
    - UnifiedWeightConverter: Handles parallelism strategy conversion
    Supports NCCL and RDMA backends for trillion-parameter sync.
  </template>
</category>

</aiml>
